  "result": "I fixed all three problems in `src/queue.js`, and `npm test` now passes with all 5 tests green.\n\n- **Hang after a failure:** a job that rejected or threw synchronously never decremented `running`, so its slot stayed taken forever. Both cases now free the slot, reject only that job's promise, and let the queue carry on.\n- **`onIdle()` resolving early:** it only checked that nothing was pending, so it fired while jobs were still running. It now also requires `running === 0`.\n- **One job at a time after `resume()`:** `resume()` started only one job. The scheduler now loops until every free slot is filled or the pending list is empty.\n\nI added three regression tests to `test/queue.test.js`:\n- A failing job, async or sync, rejects only itself and the queue continues.\n- `onIdle()` waits for jobs that are still running.\n- With concurrency 4, `resume()` starts four jobs at once.\n\nI haven't run the new tests against the old code to confirm they fail there.",
